# macOS
.DS_Store

# Terraform local artifacts
.terraform/

# Dependency lock files are deliberately NOT committed in this repo.
#
# `terraform init` writes one into the working directory, and the trailing slash
# above does not exclude it — so without this rule they get picked up by an
# unqualified `git add` and reappear one directory at a time.
#
# The decision: provider versions are controlled by required_providers in each
# example's versions.tf, pinned to patch level (`~> X.Y.0`), and nowhere else.
# That keeps one source of truth rather than two that can disagree, which is what
# was happening — deploy-runners.yml and demo-storage.yml pass `terraform init
# -upgrade`, which discards the locked version and re-resolves anyway, so the
# committed lockfiles were already decorative for those two.
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS, so nobody has to rediscover it:
#   * No checksum verification of the provider binary. The lockfile's zh:/h1:
#     hashes were the only integrity check against a corrupted or substituted
#     download.
#   * A past deploy cannot be reproduced exactly. Patch releases inside the
#     constraint will differ between runs.
#   * Every provider must be declared in a root's required_providers to be
#     bounded at all. `time` was NOT, and was pinned only by the lockfile — see
#     the note on it in access-vending-demo/versions.tf.
#
# To reverse: delete this rule, run `terraform init` then
# `terraform providers lock -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=darwin_arm64` in each
# example, commit the results, and drop `-upgrade` from the workflows so the
# lockfiles actually govern.
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Sensitive / environment-specific Terraform config (use *.example counterparts)
backend.hcl

# NOTE: terraform.tfvars is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# examples/access-vending-demo/terraform.tfvars must be committed — for an
# access-vending system the configuration IS the governance record: "who is
# systemeier for prod" and "which roles need dual approval" belong in a reviewed
# PR with history. Its deploy workflow fails fast if the file is missing.
#
# It holds no credentials: tenant_id and provider_subscription_id come from
# GitHub secrets via TF_VAR_. If you ever re-add a broad *.tfvars rule above,
# keep this exception so the access-vending deploy does not break.
!examples/access-vending-demo/terraform.tfvars

# Environment files
*.tfvars.local
*.auto.tfvars.local

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# Azure Functions local files
scaler-function/.python_packages/
scaler-function/.venv/
scaler-function/local.settings.json

# Build artifacts
*.zip

# Temporary/debug scripts
.tmp_*
_test_*.py
